#: src/internals/rfc-rooting-by-construction.md:185
msgid ""
"**The sharper finding is that all four were the same defect shape.** Every "
"one had rooting already — the pattern's root, the receiver's root, the per-"
"block unbox, the registry for registered symbols. What was missing in each "
"case was **ordering the root relative to the collection point**. That is "
"precisely the property this RFC enforces: a `Raw` that dies at the next "
"`&mut` emit makes \"used after a collection point\" unrepresentable rather "
"than reviewable."
msgstr ""
"**4つとも同じ欠陥の形でした** 各には既にルーティングがありました パターンの"
"ルーティング 受信機のルーティング ブロックごとに開箱 登録されたシンボルのレジ"
"ストリです 欠けているのは **採集点に対する根の順序**. これはまさにこのRFCが強"
"制するプロパティである.次の`&mut`送信時に消える`Raw`は\",収集ポイント後に使用"
"する\"ことをレビューできるのではなく,表現できないものにする."

#: src/internals/rfc-rooting-by-construction.md:192
msgid ""
"So the design generalises, and the open question this evidence raises is not "
"whether to adopt it for codegen, but whether layer 3 needs the same "
"discipline in `perry-runtime` — where `RuntimeHandleScope` exists (675 uses "
"across 169 files) but is **optional**, and where three of these four bugs "
"lived. A handle type that made the raw pointer unusable across an allocating "
"call would have caught all three by the same mechanism."
msgstr ""
"レイヤ3は `perry-runtime` の同じ規律が必要なのか, `RuntimeHandleScope` が存在"
"するが, **選択可能**この4つの虫のうち3匹が住んでいた場所です 配分呼び出しで使"
"用できない原始ポインタを作ったハンドルタイプは 3つとも同じメカニズムで捕まえ"
"たでしょう"

#: src/internals/rfc-rooting-by-construction.md:199
